# Normalize line endings so a Windows checkout still produces a working image.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) rewrites these files
# to CRLF on checkout. For a shell script that is fatal inside the container:
# the shebang becomes "#!/bin/bash\r" and the kernel looks for an interpreter
# literally named "bash\r", which surfaces as the very confusing
#   exec container process (missing dynamic library?) `/app/./docker-entrypoint.sh`:
#   No such file or directory
# Linux and macOS checkouts were unaffected, so this only ever bit Windows.

# Files consumed by Linux tooling — always LF, on every platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
Procfile        text eol=lf

# Let git decide for everything else.
* text=auto
